<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53074" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάνεον</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, τό, 
			Ep.
		 also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάνειον</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κανοῦν</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			12.313.136
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			22.1414.20
		</span></i>, al.; dual <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κανώ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
			12.280.10
		</span></i>; pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κανᾶ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
			22.1414.38
		</span></i>:— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>basket of
				reed</i> or <i>cane</i>, esp. <i>bread-basket</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλοῖς ἐν κανέοισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.217
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περικαλλέος ἐκ κανέοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.343
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.119
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χάλκειον κάνεον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.630
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χρύσεια κάνεια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.355
				</span></i>
			; esp. used for the sacred barley at sacrifices, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχεν οὐλὰς ἐν κανέῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.442
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κανοῦν ἐνῆρκται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					1142
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>HF</u>
				926
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.120
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Sam.</u>
				7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κανοῦν ὀλὰς ἔχον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					948
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ach.</u>
				244
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				137
			</span></i>, etc.; carried in procession, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Epit.</u>
				222
			</span></i>; as a votive offering (perh. a vessel of basketshape), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				11(2).161
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				34
			</span></i>, al. (Delos, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				7.2424
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Thebes</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				2855.21
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Branchidae</span>).</div>
